.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
The generic USB transfer structure\&. 

The user populates this structure and then submits it in order to request a transfer\&. After the transfer has completed, the library populates the transfer with the results and passes it back to the user\&. 
.SH "Field Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "unsigned int libusb_transfer::timeout"

.PP
Timeout for this transfer in milliseconds\&. A value of 0 indicates no timeout\&. 
.SS "enum \fBlibusb_transfer_status\fP libusb_transfer::status"

.PP
The status of the transfer\&. Read-only, and only for use within transfer callback function\&.

.PP
If this is an isochronous transfer, this field may read COMPLETED even if there were errors in the frames\&. Use the \fBstatus\fP field in each packet to determine if errors occurred\&. 
.SS "int libusb_transfer::length"

.PP
Length of the data buffer\&. Must be non-negative\&. 
.SS "int libusb_transfer::actual_length"

.PP
Actual length of data that was transferred\&. Read-only, and only for use within transfer callback function\&. Not valid for isochronous endpoint transfers\&. Never negative\&. 
.SS "\fBlibusb_transfer_cb_fn\fP libusb_transfer::callback"

.PP
Callback function\&. This will be invoked when the transfer completes, fails, or is cancelled\&. 
.SS "void* libusb_transfer::user_data"

.PP
User context data\&. Useful for associating specific data to a transfer that can be accessed from within the callback function\&.

.PP
This field may be set manually or is taken as the \fR\fBuser_data\fP\fP parameter of the following functions:
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBlibusb_fill_bulk_transfer()\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
